$string['materialtemplatesprompt'] = 'I want to create a reusable visual template for mod_mcp on Moodle {$a->wwwroot}, course ID {$a->courseid}, scope={$a->scope}. Before proposing anything, ask me about the visual identity, intended audience, layout, typography, spacing, cards, imagery, accessibility, dark mode and reference materials. Wait for my answers. Use live MCP tool discovery and read mcp_get_material_theme for this course to inspect existing templates. Respect the active Moodle CSS variables, including RGB tokens where applicable. Propose a name (up to 160 bytes) and reusable plain-text visual guidelines (up to 3000 bytes). Do not create or change any activity, change the Moodle interface theme, or invent a default. Explain the selected scope and show the previous template if one exists. Request my explicit approval before replacing it. Use mcp_configure_material_theme with the selected scope, name and style, and courseid for course scope. Follow the official preview and confirmation flow before saving. If site scope is not authorized, do not change the course scope without asking. Verify the saved template using mcp_get_material_theme and report the result. If the connection is unavailable, provide the name and guidelines for manual entry instead.';
